  "question": {
    "text": "Let $S$ denote the locus of the point of intersection of the pair of lines\n$4 x-3 y=12 \\alpha$\n$4 \\alpha x+3 \\alpha y=12$\nwhere $\\alpha$ varies over the set of non-zero real numbers. Let $T$ be the tangent to $S$ passing through the points $(p, 0)$ and $(0, q), q>0$, and parallel to the line $4 x-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} y=0$.<br>Then the value of $p q$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "znvoz",
      "text": "$-6 \\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
